  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Inakoti Kondala Rao vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 11 September, 2020 Author: D.Ramesh Bench: D.Ramesh The Hon'Ble Sri Justice D.Ramesh Criminal Petition No.7799 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The present criminal petition is filed to quash the proceedings in FIR No.716 of 2019 on the file of Anakapalli (T) Police Station, Visakhapatnam registered for the offences under Sections 307, 353, 270, 273, 328 read with 34 of Indian Penal Code and Section 59(1) of Food Safety Standard Act [for short FSS Act], against the petitioners/Accused No.4 and 6. 2.",
    "arguments": "3. Learned counsel for the petitioners has placed reliance on the orders of this Court, passed in Criminal Petition No.6133 of 2019, dated 25.10.2019 and the common order passed in Criminal Petition Nos.3731 of 2018 and batch, dated 27.08.2018 wherein the criminal proceedings initiated against the petitioners/accused therein are [LEAKAGE_MASK] for the offences punishable under Indian Penal Code and FSS Act holding that \"tobacco\" products would not fall within the definition of \"food\", as specified under Section 3(i)(j) of FSS Act, therefore, registration of FIR is not permissible.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. Learned counsel for the petitioners has placed reliance on the orders of this Court, passed in Criminal Petition No.6133 of 2019, dated 25.10.2019 and the common order passed in Criminal Petition Nos.3731 of 2018 and batch, dated 27.08.2018 wherein the criminal proceedings initiated against the petitioners/accused therein are [LEAKAGE_MASK] for the offences punishable under Indian Penal Code and FSS Act holding that \"tobacco\" products would not fall within the definition of \"food\", as specified under Section 3(i)(j) of FSS Act, therefore, registration of FIR is not permissible.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
